    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">What The Storm Blew In</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;Before she could open her mouth, she caught sight - no, connected with the most threatening pair of eyes she had ever seen in her life. Firey and glinting dangerously in the darkness of the noisy crowd were two eyes staring her down. One was a chilling, fierce blue like the icy slopes of the high north region; the other a wicked, fearsome amber, just like the coat of the wild beasts that lived in the deep woods.  Adora didnâ€™t spook easily, but these eyes were downright terrifying.&lt;br /&gt;â€”â€”â€”â€”â€”&lt;br /&gt;Adora leads a hard, bitter life, working the illegal nightshift at Brightmoon's harbor. On a particularly wretched night, Adora finds herself in the seediest of pubs to wallow in her pain. She is bitter as hell and aching for a fight when the perfect opportunity presents it's self....or does it? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;----&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Leathery homosexualty in a fantastical Brightmoon. Really, we just wanted a fic like this with a dark n' stormy night and GAY SHIT.&lt;br /&gt;Catra is a masculine genderfluid queer magicat - I use they/them pronouns for them.&lt;br /&gt;Adora is a butch genderfluid lesbian-type who might be described as a butch dyke, but but likeâ€¦the lines are blurry. â€œDisaster lesbianâ€ seemed like the best tag to use.&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
